WEBVTT

01:50.689 --> 01:51.924
[snarling]

01:51.957 --> 01:53.226
A Boom spell?!

01:57.001 --> 01:58.504
[roaring]

02:07.589 --> 02:08.724
Alright...

02:08.758 --> 02:09.793
You!

02:10.962 --> 02:12.431
Sizzle...

02:12.465 --> 02:13.366
Dai!

02:16.773 --> 02:17.809
[pained grunt]

02:26.325 --> 02:28.931
Dai [thought]:
This is impossible...

02:28.964 --> 02:30.801
Baran [thought]:
We won't win this way.

02:31.637 --> 02:33.406
Kasizz!

03:18.430 --> 03:21.303
Draconic Aura defense.
Interesting.

03:21.336 --> 03:23.373
Like father, like son.

03:23.406 --> 03:26.747
Vearn: Baran has
realized that Hadlar's body

03:26.780 --> 03:29.451
contains a Black Core.

03:29.485 --> 03:32.190
Do you see it now,
Mystvearn?

03:32.224 --> 03:35.230
Hadlar may actually
have a chance.

03:35.264 --> 03:37.669
The attacks and spells
of these Dragon Knights

03:37.702 --> 03:40.173
are too powerful,
aren't they?

03:40.206 --> 03:42.779
They're afraid it
will detonate.

03:42.813 --> 03:44.516
It is an advantage-

03:44.549 --> 03:48.189
it's keeping them from
fighting at full strength.

03:48.223 --> 03:49.526
Mystvearn: Cowards!

03:50.595 --> 03:52.999
Hadlar: Why are you
holding back?

03:53.033 --> 03:54.903
Don't tell me you've
lost your nerve.

03:54.936 --> 03:58.409
What happened to the great
"Dragon Knights" of old?

03:59.211 --> 04:00.548
Father and son.

04:00.581 --> 04:03.286
Don't you know how
to fight together?

04:03.320 --> 04:06.760
Baran, where's
your Gigabreak?!

04:08.731 --> 04:13.974
And Dai - you, too. Don't you
want to avenge your old master?

04:14.008 --> 04:15.143
Here's your chance.

04:15.176 --> 04:18.717
Go ahead and try to
take your revenge on me.

04:25.363 --> 04:27.903
Dai [thought]: That's it!
Hadlar doesn't know.

04:27.936 --> 04:31.008
Maybe if I tell him,
he'll stop fighting.

04:32.578 --> 04:33.814
Listen, Hadlar!
You've got-

04:33.847 --> 04:34.716
Baran: Don't.

04:35.785 --> 04:37.354
You mustn't tell him.

04:37.388 --> 04:39.592
Dai: Huh? Why not?!

04:39.626 --> 04:41.897
Baran: A Black Core
can be detonated

04:41.930 --> 04:44.268
at the whim of it's creator.

04:44.301 --> 04:47.207
Once Hadlar knows it's there,

04:47.241 --> 04:50.547
Vearn will activate
it on the spot.

04:50.581 --> 04:54.822
He'll do it just to keep Hadlar
from turning against him.

04:57.294 --> 04:58.630
What's wrong?

04:59.465 --> 05:01.002
Baran: We'll be fine.

05:01.035 --> 05:05.611
If we focus all our energy on
defense, we should survive.

05:05.645 --> 05:11.255
But your friends on the surface
will almost certainly perish.

05:11.289 --> 05:13.560
Hadlar: Don't
insult me like this.

05:14.228 --> 05:15.598
Dai [thought]: At this rate...

05:15.631 --> 05:20.040
Hadlar: How very suspicious.
What are you up to?

05:20.073 --> 05:22.177
Just you wait and see!

05:22.210 --> 05:23.547
Baran: Zapple!

05:32.632 --> 05:36.205
Fight me. I've seen
you in action, Hadlar.

05:36.238 --> 05:38.409
So I know the
extent of your power.

05:38.443 --> 05:42.051
As you requested of me,
I will draw my blade.

05:42.084 --> 05:46.960
Interesting. So you were just
testing me this whole time?

05:46.994 --> 05:48.463
That's good to hear.

05:48.497 --> 05:50.233
Dai: What are you doing?!

05:50.266 --> 05:53.372
Baran: I'm going to
have him explode here.

05:53.406 --> 05:56.780
It's a risk,
but I have no choice.

05:56.813 --> 05:57.448
Dai: What?!

05:57.481 --> 05:58.784
Baran: If I decapitate him,

05:58.817 --> 06:02.559
he shouldn't
detonate right away.

06:02.592 --> 06:07.267
It will take a moment for Vearn
to realize what's happened.

06:07.300 --> 06:10.307
That's when I'll use
all of my Draconic Aura

06:10.340 --> 06:13.413
available to
contain the blast.

06:13.446 --> 06:15.450
Dai: But you don't
know that'll work!

06:15.483 --> 06:16.786
What makes you think it can

06:16.820 --> 06:18.991
be contained by
a Draconic Aura?

06:19.024 --> 06:21.062
Even one like yours?!

06:21.095 --> 06:23.700
It's way too dangerous!

06:32.518 --> 06:38.029
Baran: Dai... Tell me.
Do you trust me?

06:45.076 --> 06:46.145
Baran: Well?

06:49.786 --> 06:53.727
Dai: I... I trust your
strength more than anyone's.

06:55.230 --> 06:56.633
Baran: A good answer.

06:56.666 --> 06:59.539
And I trust your
strength as well.

07:01.042 --> 07:03.614
Seeing you fight against
the Bishop and Hadlar

07:03.647 --> 07:05.584
has made me realize...

07:05.618 --> 07:08.890
You're far stronger than
when you last fought me.

07:10.594 --> 07:13.032
I'm impressed
with how you've grown.

07:14.636 --> 07:17.608
Baran: But this is
something only I can do...

07:17.642 --> 07:21.583
With my sword skills and
abundance of Draconic Aura.

07:21.616 --> 07:24.622
So I'm going to
need you to trust me.

07:26.358 --> 07:27.896
And get your
friends out of here,

07:27.929 --> 07:30.668
just in case
things go poorly.

07:31.836 --> 07:34.542
Take that hole to the surface.

07:35.678 --> 07:37.414
Baran: No matter
what happens to me,

07:37.448 --> 07:40.588
I promise I'll
take care of Hadlar.

07:40.621 --> 07:43.660
I leave the fight
with King Vearn to you.

07:43.693 --> 07:47.568
Dai, I truly hope
that you win.

07:47.602 --> 07:52.210
For you... and for
those who believe in you.

07:54.783 --> 07:55.818
[growling]

07:55.852 --> 08:04.201
[roaring]

08:06.372 --> 08:07.708
[chuckling]

08:07.742 --> 08:11.115
What impressive
power we wield.

08:11.149 --> 08:14.421
You have your Ultimate
Blade and Gigabreak...

08:14.455 --> 08:18.730
And I have my Ultra
Combustion Slash!

08:18.764 --> 08:22.404
Both infuse our blades
with supercharged energy

08:22.438 --> 08:26.880
to destroy our enemies
at the moment of impact.

08:26.913 --> 08:31.222
So that means, the first
to land a hit wins.

08:31.255 --> 08:35.463
It seems all will be
decided by who is fastest!

08:35.496 --> 08:37.768
Yes... It will.

08:37.802 --> 08:41.977
Hadlar: I doubt that either of
us will require a second strike.

08:42.010 --> 08:46.051
Both attacks are strong
enough to end everything.

08:46.085 --> 08:50.460
Dai [thought]: Maybe...
Maybe I should help him.

08:50.494 --> 08:53.466
Maybe I can use my
own Draconic Aura...

08:53.499 --> 08:55.638
to help contain the blast...

08:55.671 --> 08:58.711
Baran: Do not interfere!

08:58.744 --> 09:01.448
Baran: What Hadlar said
is absolutely right.

09:01.482 --> 09:02.886
The timing is everything.

09:02.919 --> 09:07.261
If you interfere, it increases
my chances of failing.

09:07.294 --> 09:08.897
Dai: B-But... I...

09:08.931 --> 09:13.740
Baran: Dai... Didn't you say
that you trust my strength?

09:17.147 --> 09:18.015
Dai: All right!

09:18.049 --> 09:20.420
But once Popp and
the others are safe,

09:20.453 --> 09:22.157
I'm coming back to help.

09:23.560 --> 09:27.167
Promise me... you won't fail.

09:28.703 --> 09:33.078
Baran: Yes. You have my word.

09:34.615 --> 09:36.252
Get to safety.

09:36.285 --> 09:37.955
Hadlar? It's time!

09:37.989 --> 09:41.563
Show me a Dragon
Knight's true power!

09:41.596 --> 09:42.932
Baran: Go, Dai!

09:45.538 --> 09:46.706
Gigabreak!

09:46.739 --> 09:49.144
Hadlar: Ultra
Combustion Slash!

09:50.046 --> 09:51.381
Got you!

09:53.419 --> 09:54.321
What?

09:55.389 --> 09:56.659
Baran: Hadlar...

09:56.693 --> 09:58.362
It's over!

10:00.400 --> 10:02.036
H-He did it!

10:03.339 --> 10:04.241
[shocked gasp]

10:05.076 --> 10:06.378
But, how?!

10:06.411 --> 10:08.115
Baran: It didn't cut through!

10:09.519 --> 10:10.587
Look out!

10:10.621 --> 10:12.658
[roaring]

10:16.365 --> 10:18.369
D-Dai?!

10:23.479 --> 10:24.882
Dino!

11:02.157 --> 11:03.192
Move!

11:05.463 --> 11:06.265
Dino!

11:06.299 --> 11:07.502
Dino, you have to wake up!

11:07.535 --> 11:08.637
Please!

11:08.670 --> 11:11.141
Baran [thought]: No!
The wound is too deep.

11:11.174 --> 11:14.783
Left untreated,
it could be fatal!

11:14.816 --> 11:17.186
Dai: [pained groaning]

11:17.955 --> 11:19.024
Dino...

11:20.493 --> 11:24.869
Who? Oh, right.
Y-You mean me.

11:24.903 --> 11:28.175
Looks... like the
attack didn't work.

11:28.208 --> 11:30.379
It-It's strange.

11:30.413 --> 11:33.419
When you first fought me,
your Gigabreak...

11:33.452 --> 11:36.793
It seemed a whole
lot stronger...

11:38.429 --> 11:40.366
That's enough. Don't talk.

11:40.399 --> 11:42.170
Let's get you healed up first.

11:45.376 --> 11:46.980
Hadlar [thought]: How?

11:47.014 --> 11:49.919
Nothing should have been
able to survive that.

11:49.952 --> 11:52.858
Baran's attack was
perfectly timed-

11:52.892 --> 11:55.396
and at the optimal range.

11:55.430 --> 11:59.639
How could I withstand a strike
from the Dragon Master...

11:59.672 --> 12:02.310
and endure it so easily?

12:03.445 --> 12:04.849
Hadlar: How?!

12:05.984 --> 12:10.059
Killvearn: Allow me
to answer that question.

12:10.093 --> 12:11.295
Killvearn!

12:11.329 --> 12:12.865
Baran: You're still alive?

12:13.634 --> 12:15.069
Killvearn: [chuckling]

12:15.103 --> 12:18.343
It'd be a pretty sad world if
even a reaper could be killed.

12:18.376 --> 12:19.913
Of course, I'm alive.

12:19.946 --> 12:22.150
Yeah! The undying man!

12:22.183 --> 12:26.425
But how? When I left you...
you were in pieces!

12:26.458 --> 12:27.829
Killvearn: That's the thing.

12:27.862 --> 12:30.801
You took your eyes off
me too soon, Baran.

12:30.834 --> 12:32.203
How's that?

12:32.237 --> 12:34.942
Killvearn: The blood in my
veins has the same composition

12:34.976 --> 12:37.314
as Underworld magma.

12:37.347 --> 12:42.625
It's extremely hot and
contains a powerful acid.

12:42.658 --> 12:47.568
And you went and cut me in half
- very painful, by the way -

12:47.601 --> 12:52.678
but getting my blood all over
your Demon Dragon Blade.

12:52.712 --> 12:56.351
So, you see, my blood
corroded your weapon,

12:56.385 --> 13:01.061
and dulled the edge of
your incredible blade.

13:01.095 --> 13:04.334
Even the Demon Dragon
Blade can't regenerate

13:04.367 --> 13:07.675
from that kind of
damage so quickly.

13:07.708 --> 13:10.313
Against someone as
strong as Hadlar here,

13:10.347 --> 13:14.856
it completely loses
its effectiveness.

13:14.889 --> 13:18.262
This is my curse, Baran.

13:18.295 --> 13:19.766
You may evade me,

13:19.799 --> 13:23.272
but there are consequences
for all actions.

13:23.305 --> 13:28.182
A reaper always gets
their target in the end.

13:28.215 --> 13:31.288
So there you have it, Hadlar.

13:31.322 --> 13:34.094
I doubt you'd like
me taking your prey,

13:34.127 --> 13:36.198
I'll leave the rest to you.

13:36.232 --> 13:39.705
Be sure to take
care of him for me.

13:39.739 --> 13:42.143
Reaper. I was not
aware that you were

13:42.177 --> 13:45.149
under orders to
eliminate Baran.

13:45.182 --> 13:48.289
It's all cloak and
dagger with you.

13:48.322 --> 13:50.661
Killvearn:
That's an ugly wound.

13:50.694 --> 13:52.932
Piroro! Tend to him, will you?

13:52.965 --> 13:54.735
No. It'll heal.

13:54.769 --> 13:58.142
Piroro: Now, now.
Don't be like that.

13:58.175 --> 14:02.017
Killvearn: Learn to accept
people's generosity, Hadlar.

14:02.050 --> 14:04.320
So long as our friend
Baran is eliminated,

14:04.354 --> 14:07.895
my job will be
considered complete.

14:07.928 --> 14:10.066
One more thing.

14:10.099 --> 14:14.509
I'd advise against showing
these two any mercy.

14:14.542 --> 14:16.813
You should crush them at once.

14:16.847 --> 14:18.583
You may want a fair fight,

14:18.617 --> 14:22.290
but his sword won't
regenerate for quite a while.

14:22.323 --> 14:25.630
Do you have that
sort of time left?

14:26.833 --> 14:27.835
How did you...?

14:27.868 --> 14:30.273
Hooray! It's all healed now.

14:30.306 --> 14:33.647
Oh wait. There's another
wound over here.

14:33.680 --> 14:34.682
[alarmed breath]

14:34.716 --> 14:36.519
Piroro: Let me take
care of that...

14:41.261 --> 14:42.497
[evil laughter]

14:43.199 --> 14:44.602
Baran [thought]: They know.

14:44.635 --> 14:48.042
They're not backing down so
that Hadlar can have the glory;

14:48.075 --> 14:51.950
they want to avoid
the Black Core's explosion!

14:51.983 --> 14:54.889
Killvearn: Goodbye
and good luck, Hadlar.

14:54.923 --> 14:58.296
You too, Baran.
Not that it'll help.

14:58.329 --> 14:59.397
[giggle]

15:00.667 --> 15:04.207
I'd prefer to win this
without Killvearn's help.

15:04.240 --> 15:07.347
But I don't have the
luxury of waiting until

15:07.380 --> 15:10.319
you both are ready
to fight again.

15:10.353 --> 15:14.294
So I won't be
holding back, Baran.

15:14.327 --> 15:17.735
Baran [thought]: No...
If I stop the healing spell now,

15:17.768 --> 15:19.404
Dino might not survive!

15:19.437 --> 15:23.412
I can't let go of him, no
matter what attack may come.

15:25.249 --> 15:27.621
You choose to protect the boy.

15:27.654 --> 15:29.091
Well, so be it.

15:29.124 --> 15:32.532
I can't extend the
inevitable any longer.

15:32.565 --> 15:35.269
Let us finish this at last.

15:36.973 --> 15:39.077
D-Dodge it!

15:39.111 --> 15:42.584
Forget about me.
Keep fighting.

15:45.323 --> 15:46.993
Kaboom!

16:06.566 --> 16:07.433
Dino!

16:11.375 --> 16:15.182
H-How could you...
be so... so reckless?!

16:18.824 --> 16:20.961
I'm fine. I can fight.

16:20.995 --> 16:24.367
Somehow I'm already
fully healed.

16:24.401 --> 16:26.138
[wincing]

16:26.172 --> 16:28.610
Stop pretending! You can
barely hold yourself up.

16:28.643 --> 16:29.478
That's enough.

16:29.512 --> 16:31.115
What?

16:31.148 --> 16:33.252
Dai: All of this
covering for each other,

16:33.285 --> 16:37.159
and walking on eggshells
while we're trying to fight...

16:38.362 --> 16:39.431
I've had it!

16:39.464 --> 16:43.305
We're... family,
isn't that right?

16:44.007 --> 16:45.945
Dino...

16:45.978 --> 16:48.984
If we're gonna fight
together... then trust me.

16:49.017 --> 16:52.089
Trust that the two
of us can fight as one!

16:52.123 --> 16:55.597
If we learn to respect
each other, then who knows?

16:55.630 --> 16:57.333
Maybe we can...

16:57.367 --> 17:01.174
find a power truly
worth fighting for.

17:01.809 --> 17:03.680
A new power...

17:06.953 --> 17:09.625
Okay. Here we go, Hadlar!

17:13.834 --> 17:15.135
Darn it...

17:15.737 --> 17:18.275
I can do this!

17:18.309 --> 17:21.515
Hadlar [thought]: He
possesses such unlimited will.

17:37.414 --> 17:41.590
Baran: Very well.
I'll do as you say.

17:41.623 --> 17:42.524
Really?

17:44.729 --> 17:46.533
What... was that?!

17:46.566 --> 17:47.769
Baran: Dai.

17:47.802 --> 17:49.003
I meant to ask you...

17:49.037 --> 17:51.141
who was it that
gave you that name?

17:51.175 --> 17:54.247
It was Grampa Brass.

17:54.281 --> 17:58.021
When I washed up on
Dermline Island.

17:58.055 --> 17:59.124
My crib...

17:59.158 --> 18:02.363
It had a name plate.

18:02.397 --> 18:05.737
Only the letter "D"
was left on it.

18:05.770 --> 18:09.444
Grampa gave me this
name so that at least...

18:09.477 --> 18:13.251
I'd have the initial
my real parents gave me.

18:19.264 --> 18:21.535
Why am I so sleepy?

18:21.569 --> 18:25.711
That is the sleep spell,
Kasnooze. I cast it on you.

18:25.744 --> 18:30.219
So just leave the fighting to
me and get some rest, okay?

18:30.253 --> 18:33.258
But why?
I would fight with you.

18:33.292 --> 18:35.965
Lie still and let
yourself heal, son.

18:35.998 --> 18:38.536
Dragon Knights have
unmatched abilities.

18:38.569 --> 18:42.077
We can heal faster
than others can.

18:42.110 --> 18:46.218
How could... how could
you do this to me?

18:46.251 --> 18:47.921
You may wish otherwise,

18:47.954 --> 18:52.096
but I now realize that this
is what a parent must do.

18:52.130 --> 18:55.370
You will understand
when you grow up.

18:55.403 --> 18:57.373
Please, don't do this!

18:57.406 --> 19:00.781
I'll fight...
I'll fight with you...

19:00.814 --> 19:03.151
"Dai", huh?

19:04.120 --> 19:06.424
It's a good name.

19:06.458 --> 19:11.034
But I hope you'll remember the
name that Soala and I gave you.

19:11.068 --> 19:17.179
"Dino". In the Alkeed language
it means, "Strong Dragon".

19:18.884 --> 19:20.386
But, why?

19:20.420 --> 19:24.628
Why does everybody pull
the same trick on me?

19:24.661 --> 19:26.097
Even Master...

19:26.131 --> 19:30.472
Even Master cast Kaclang
on me, and then he...

19:30.974 --> 19:32.309
I see.

19:32.343 --> 19:35.917
So Avan used the
same sort of tactic.

19:36.853 --> 19:37.788
Well, then.

19:37.822 --> 19:39.525
It seems as if I...

19:39.558 --> 19:42.899
maybe a little too late
for it to change things...

19:42.932 --> 19:45.302
I did learn to be human.

19:46.004 --> 19:48.108
Dai: This can't be the end!

19:48.141 --> 19:49.645
It can't be...

19:50.714 --> 19:52.718
N-No...

19:52.751 --> 19:54.287
It's not...

19:54.989 --> 19:56.625
It's not...

19:59.064 --> 20:00.299
fair.

20:04.508 --> 20:07.814
Baran: Come on!
Good night, Dino.

20:09.184 --> 20:11.355
Go to sleep.

20:11.388 --> 20:17.935
Baby Dai: [crying]

20:17.968 --> 20:19.905
Come on, Dino!

20:21.041 --> 20:22.979
What's wrong, son?

20:23.012 --> 20:23.980
[sigh]

20:24.013 --> 20:26.451
Baran. You're doing it wrong.

20:26.484 --> 20:29.958
Go to sleep, Dino.
Sweet dreams.

20:31.094 --> 20:32.698
It just takes some time.

20:32.731 --> 20:35.871
I'm pretty sure you'll get
the hang of it, someday!

20:35.904 --> 20:38.810
Baran [thought]: It looks
like you were right, Soala.

20:41.883 --> 20:45.657
I never did get the hang
of putting him to sleep.

20:55.409 --> 21:00.019
Well, look at you. A true
parent at heart, Baran.

21:00.053 --> 21:02.423
Prepare yourself, Hadlar.

21:02.457 --> 21:06.532
I swore I'd never use
this power again, but...

21:06.566 --> 21:09.437
You've left me no choice.

21:10.272 --> 21:11.809
Hadlar: That's...

21:13.079 --> 21:17.153
Believe me, I didn't put Dino
to sleep for his well being...

21:17.187 --> 21:21.896
I took this terrible form when
we last battled each other...

21:23.299 --> 21:26.404
I never want Dino to
see it again!

21:32.016 --> 21:33.318
Your true form!

21:33.351 --> 21:34.922
The Dragonoid!

21:40.533 --> 21:41.903
Hadlar: [laughing]

21:41.936 --> 21:42.905
I see.

21:42.938 --> 21:44.274
So you plan to fight in

21:44.307 --> 21:47.781
the Dragon Knight's
ultimate battle mode!

21:47.815 --> 21:50.987
Then fine. I accept
your challenge!

21:53.994 --> 21:58.770
Well, Hadlar? The two of
us can go to hell together!

21:58.803 --> 22:02.544
[excruciated howl]

22:02.578 --> 22:04.514
Hadlar: C-Curse you!

23:37.768 --> 23:40.840
Narrator: While the Disciples
of Avan battle the Royal Guard,

23:40.874 --> 23:43.680
Baran assumes his
Dragonoid form once again

23:43.713 --> 23:45.984
and faces off against Hadlar.

23:46.017 --> 23:48.789
With the fate of his
son hanging in the balance,

23:48.823 --> 23:51.662
Baran unleashes
his full fury...

23:51.695 --> 23:54.000
But King Vearn
watches from his throne,

23:54.034 --> 23:57.172
and could detonate his
henchman at any moment.

23:57.206 --> 23:58.676
So don't miss
the next episode of

23:58.709 --> 24:01.248
Dragon Quest:
The Adventure of Dai,

24:01.281 --> 24:03.552
"The Black Core."
